   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Regular formation of the future",
     "texto": [
      "In Italian, the three regular conjugations form the future on a base with **-r-** followed by the same endings for all verbs: **-ò, -ai, -à, -emo, -ete, -anno**.",
      "Verbs in **-are** change the thematic **-a-** to **-e-** (*parlare → parlerò, parlerai, parlerà...*), as do verbs in **-ere** (*prendere → prenderò...*). Verbs in **-ire** keep their **-i-** (*dormire → dormirò...*)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Compulsory written accent",
     "texto": [
      "Remember that the first person singular (**-ò**) and the third person singular (**-à**) always carry a grave written accent: **parlerò**, **sentirà**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
